ccurred in the number of reported measles cases\"}]}, {\"v\": \"evaluation or monitoring\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The quality of measles case-based surveillance is monitored by two key indicators\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"the percentage of suspected measles cases with a blood specimen (24% in 2004; target: 80%)\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The administrative method for estimating vaccination coverage is calculated by dividing the reported number of vaccine doses administered\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Comparing the reported incidence before and after the June 2003 SIA (i.e., 2002 versus 2004)\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The quality of measles case-based surveillance is monitored by two key indicators\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\"]}", "type": "text"}]}